From b214601d125408061888a5fbb4ba6814df37138f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iain Sandoe <iain@sandoe.co.uk>
Date: Fri, 12 Apr 2024 09:23:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/97] collect2, Darwin: Support -fuse-ld=lld.

The lld project has some support for Mach-o/Darwin but the linker
name must be adjusted (so that Mach-O-specific command line syntax
is accepted).

In general, linkers used on Darwin do not accept or understand
fuse-ld= options, so we need to strip those from the command line in
collect-ld.  Since this must operate using /bin/sh, we need to amend
the handling of the args to implement this.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* collect2.cc (LLD_NAME): New.
	(main): Do not accept BFD or Gold linkers for Mach-O.
	* config/darwin.h (DARWIN_NOCOMPACT_UNWIND): Do not emit
	-no_compact_unwind for lld.
	* configure: Regenerate.
	* configure.ac: Build a path to ld64.lld (for Darwin) or
	lld (otherwise).
	* exec-tool.in: Amend to handle the fuse-ld=lld option.

Signed-off-by: Iain Sandoe <iain@sandoe.co.uk>
---
