From 1cb9004d4ed9c64cbafae522694aea8909f97519 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iain Sandoe <iain@sandoe.co.uk>
Date: Sun, 29 Oct 2023 23:21:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 49/97] call-lowering: Allow promote_function_mode to depend on
 cumulative args.

TODO: make a much longer explanation of the changes....

For at least one ABI the promotion rules for small integers (QI, HI)
depend on whether the argument will be passed in register or on the stack.

This change permits the target to make such an adjustment, with a default
implementation to behave the same as currently.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* calls.cc (initialize_argument_information): Use argument
	promotion with cumulative args available.
	(emit_library_call_value_1): Likewise.
	* config/aarch64/aarch64.cc
	(aarch64_function_arg_alignment): Mach-O may have promoted argument
	modes when considering alignment.
	(aarch64_darwin_promote_fn_mode): New.
	(aarch64_darwin_promote_function_mode_ca): New.
	* config/aarch64/darwin.h (TARGET_PROMOTE_FUNCTION_MODE): New.
	(TARGET_PROMOTE_FUNCTION_MODE_CA): New.
	* doc/tm.texi: Document TARGET_PROMOTE_FUNCTION_MODE_CA.
	* doc/tm.texi.in: Likewise.
	* explow.cc (promote_function_mode): Add an overload taking a
	cumulative args input.
	* explow.h (promote_function_mode): New overload.
	* function.cc (assign_parm_find_data_types): Use argument
	promotion with cumulative args available.
	* target.def (PROMOTE_FUNCTION_MODE_CA): New hook.
	* targhooks.cc (default_promote_function_mode_ca): New.
	* targhooks.h (default_promote_function_mode_ca): New.

Signed-off-by: Iain Sandoe <iain@sandoe.co.uk>

(cherry picked from commit da862bea4e57d6125afa4ab85baf879e3ee9dec1)
