From 51048e1a40b08ae7fa98565f59c4790f277f920a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francois-Xavier Coudert <fxcoudert@gcc.gnu.org>
Date: Thu, 7 Sep 2023 07:33:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 60/97] aarch64, Darwin: Support IEEE754 Quad Precision as
 __float128.

aarch64-apple-darwin has a C long double type which is the same as the
double. In order to support a higher precision floating point type,
similarly to x86_64-apple-darwin, we define define __float128 (and
_Float128).

Co-authored-by: Iain Sandoe <iain@sandoe.co.uk>
Signed-off-by: Iain Sandoe <iain@sandoe.co.uk>

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/aarch64/aarch64-builtins.cc (AARCH64_BUILTIN_HUGE_VALQ,
	AARCH64_BUILTIN_INFQ): New built-ins.
	(aarch64_init_float128_types): New function...
	(aarch64_general_init_builtins): ... called here.
	(aarch64_general_fold_builtin): Initialize the new built-ins.
	* config/aarch64/aarch64.cc (aarch64_gimplify_va_arg_expr):
	Handle __float128 on darwin.
	(aarch64_mangle_type): Mangle __float128.
	(aarch64_c_mode_for_suffix): Assign suffix q to __float128.
	(aarch64_scalar_mode_supported_p): Ensure TFmode is allowed.
	* config/aarch64/aarch64.h (aarch64_float128_ptr_type_node): New
	node.
	* ginclude/stddef.h (__max_align_f128): Ensure it has correct
	alignment.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* g++.target/aarch64/float128-darwin-1.C: New test.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/darwin/float128-01.c: New test.

libgcc/ChangeLog:

	* config.host: Enable soft-float.
	* config/aarch64/sfp-machine.h: Provide definitions for
	aarch64-apple-darwin.
	* config/aarch64/t-darwin: Fix comment.

(cherry picked from commit 509899a70c0465900632a6237a25cd7d19f1118e)
