From 498ee84ab0c58c3073c980e062f88ab9081e5254 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iain Sandoe <iain@sandoe.co.uk>
Date: Fri, 13 Oct 2023 19:42:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 72/97] testsuite, aarch64, darwin: Handle heap trampline case.

Darwin does not create the trampoline initializer in the TU, it is
done on demand by the builtins.

(cherry picked from commit f1eb88d70682035046e89cad320e13bb5ff4cf60)
---
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/aarch64/bti-4.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/aarch64/bti-4.c b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/aarch64/bti-4.c
index 28495a5c199..109ab60fcb7 100644
--- a/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/aarch64/bti-4.c
+++ b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/aarch64/bti-4.c
@@ -56,5 +56,7 @@ retbr_trampolines2 (void *a, int b)
   return 0;
 }
 
-/* Trampoline should have BTI C. */
-/* { dg-final { scan-assembler "\.LTRAMP0:\n\thint\t34" } } */
+/* Trampoline should have BTI C.
+   but Darwin trampolines are constructed on demand by a builtin and do not
+   appear in the generated code for this TU.  */
+/* { dg-final { scan-assembler "\.LTRAMP0:\n\thint\t34" { target { ! *-*-darwin* } } } } */
-- 
2.43.0


From aa0cd5888926abbf51e17934145cc16d55a5c989 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iain Sandoe <iain@sandoe.co.uk>
Date: Fri, 13 Oct 2023 19:47:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 73/97] testsuite, aarch64, Darwin: Use __float128 instead of
 long double

Darwin's long double is the same as double, so use __float128 there to
test the same codegen as Linux.

(cherry picked from commit 534e71f4aa7e6b88089ec4ed11162c71ac329991)
---
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/aarch64/fmovld-zero-mem.c | 8 +++++++-
