From ee0e1972ae3390b422126713d84448ea4825b0b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iain Sandoe <iain@sandoe.co.uk>
Date: Sat, 14 Oct 2023 14:21:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 74/97] testsuite, aarch64, Darwin: Allow unwind frames.

Darwin's function body scan code needs the function start and end
markers which are enabled by frames (either unwind or debug).  In the
absence of these, it's not clear how we'd delinate functions, since
Mach-O does not use .size.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/aarch64/tbz_1.c: Allow unwind frames for Darwin.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/tbz_2.c: Likewise.

